    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        930.028273710284,
        392.8481290156434
      ],
      "size": [
        560,
        400
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 2,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Krea 2 Turbo \u2014 2-Step Distillation LoRA\n\nKrea 2 Turbo normally runs at 8 steps. With this community-trained LoRA it runs at **2** \u2014 a few-second generation at a fraction of the compute, without giving up much quality.\n\nLoRA by **lvladikov**: https://huggingface.co/lvladikov/Krea2-Turbo-Distill-2step-LoRA\n\n### Files (this workflow's defaults)\n- [krea2_turbo_fp8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/AlperKTS/Krea2_FP8/tree/main) -> `models/diffusion_models/` (or a [GGUF quant](https://huggingface.co/vantagewithai/Krea-2-Turbo-GGUF/tree/main) -> `models/unet/`)\n- [qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen3-VL/tree/main/text_encoders) -> `models/text_encoders/`\n- [qwen_image_vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image_ComfyUI/tree/main/split_files/vae) -> `models/vae/`\n- [krea2_turbo_2step_rank_64_lora_comfyui.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/lvladikov/Krea2-Turbo-Distill-2step-LoRA/tree/main) -> `models/loras/`\n\nSet the CLIPLoader **type to `krea2`**.\n\n### Settings\n- **steps 2**, **cfg 1.0** (Turbo is CFG-free)\n- LoRA strength **1.0**\n- The negative is a `ConditioningZeroOut` \u2014 nothing to write in it at cfg 1.0\n- The workflow ships an FP8 default plus a GGUF loader path \u2014 toggle with the Fast Groups Bypasser\n- Upscale nodes included for a clean high-res pass\n\nThis LoRA is an ongoing training run \u2014 full detail and evaluation on lvladikov's repo."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Krea 2 Turbo \u2014 2-Step Distillation LoRA\n\nKrea 2 Turbo normally runs at 8 steps. With this community-trained LoRA it runs at **2** \u2014 a few-second generation at a fraction of the compute, without giving up much quality.\n\nLoRA by **lvladikov**: https://huggingface.co/lvladikov/Krea2-Turbo-Distill-2step-LoRA\n\n### Files (this workflow's defaults)\n- [krea2_turbo_fp8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/AlperKTS/Krea2_FP8/tree/main) -> `models/diffusion_models/` (or a [GGUF quant](https://huggingface.co/vantagewithai/Krea-2-Turbo-GGUF/tree/main) -> `models/unet/`)\n- [qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen3-VL/tree/main/text_encoders) -> `models/text_encoders/`\n- [qwen_image_vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image_ComfyUI/tree/main/split_files/vae) -> `models/vae/`\n- [krea2_turbo_2step_rank_64_lora_comfyui.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/lvladikov/Krea2-Turbo-Distill-2step-LoRA/tree/main) -> `models/loras/`\n\nSet the CLIPLoader **type to `krea2`**.\n\n### Settings\n- **steps 2**, **cfg 1.0** (Turbo is CFG-free)\n- LoRA strength **1.0**\n- The negative is a `ConditioningZeroOut` \u2014 nothing to write in it at cfg 1.0\n- The workflow ships an FP8 default plus a GGUF loader path \u2014 toggle with the Fast Groups Bypasser\n- Upscale nodes included for a clean high-res pass\n\nThis LoRA is an ongoing training run \u2014 full detail and evaluation on lvladikov's repo."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
